--
-- THE ROOT CAUSE OF THE WRECKS (prod, read-only, 2026-11-14, head 0407): all 7 pirate ships lay UNABLE_TO_SAIL at hull 0.
--   WHY HULL 0: the navy's hunt (0340, public.navy_hunt_pass). Every one of the last 12 navy fights kept in public.navy_fight_log ended A_TOOK: a galion
--   (attack 250, hull 2,800) takes a lone xebec (60, 530) every time. Ship 1 was wrecked 22 times in four days; her "quiet voyage" of 06:54 UTC was
--   fought at sea at 06:49 by Navy ship 3 (a navy fight is no day of a voyage, so her report says nothing) and again at 07:50 lying at Paramaribo.
--   WHY SHE STAYS: 0339 gave a pirate ship 0322's refit ("REFIT from her home's purse", public.npc_refit_step: the home alone pays 25 % of her build
--   cost, 40,000, to the nearest yard), and 0338 founded three of the four homes with a purse of 0. Djerba had a surplus of 38,177, Goto 1,603, Lingga
--   62: under 40,000, with nobody behind them. Five ships waited REFIT_WAITING "broke" (the only rows of public.npc_refit_waits; no merchant, cargo
--   ship or navy ship was in it). Port Royal could pay, so ship 1 was refitted 27 times (1,080,000 to Santiago's yard) and taken again each time.
-- THE FIX, AT THAT CAUSE: a pirate wreck is no longer 0322's. Her own step (public.pirate_ship_step) hands her to public.pirate_reborn: she is at
--   her HOME CITY at once (voyage.npc_wreck, as before), lies pirate_respawn_minutes (60), and is then mended (public.fleet_mend), manned from her
--   home's quay (public.fleet_hands) and stored (public.fleet_stores), and sails again. WHO PAYS the refit (public.npc_refit_cost, to the yard
--   public.refit_yard names, as 0322): her own purse; else her home city; else another city the pirates hold, the richest first; else Port Royal's
--   hoard through public.pirate_pay (inside the day's room). Whole or nothing, moved, never minted. When every pirate purse is dry she waits at home
--   (WAITING, a REFIT_WAITING event once a day, a row in public.npc_refit_waits) and is asked again every time her step runs.
--   public.npc_refit_step answers NOT_A_WRECK for a pirate ship, so she is never paid for twice.
--
-- WHAT ELSE LANDS
--   * FIVE HARBOURS, held by the pirates (not homes: a home is one of four, docs/INFLUENCE.md D1; so they tax, regenerate and can be contested as any
--     city): Pitcairn (PTC, South Pacific), Midway (MWY, North Pacific), Tristan (TDC, South Atlantic), Flores (FLO, North Atlantic), Diego Garcia
--     (DGA, Indian Ocean). A data slice as 0338's three: tier 3, four existing goods each, purse 0, no seed, no gold made; roadstead and sailed
--     distances to and from every place; merchant courses to and from the nearest harbours; a market row for every good; buildings, works, flag,
--     tongue, people; the pair table's rows (the seas of the plotted course, data/sea-legs.json).
--   * public.pirate_hubs: one row a hub (its ground, the ships ordered for it, how far its ships cruise). public.pirate_roster and
--     public.pirate_roster_hulls: THE FLEETS THE PIRATES KEEP BEYOND public.pirate_size(), as data: /*NFLEETS*/ fleets, /*NSHIPS*/ ships (Pacific 70, all homed at Pitcairn so that they
--     roam the SOUTH Pacific; Midway is the North Pacific haven, a pirate city that pays in its turn, with no fleet homed there until a roster row says so; South Atlantic 40; North Atlantic 40; Indian 30). Half the fleets are one small ship, a third a xebec or a pair, a sixth a squadron
--     of four behind a lead ship; one or two houses a hub run two fleets. A count is changed by changing rows, with no new function.
--   * public.pirate_ships: a house may own several fleets (the unique key on player_id goes), and `wrecked_at` (when she was brought home a wreck).
--   * A roster fleet is built by public.pirate_commission_fleet (the hoard pays every hull's build cost to the nearest yard, public.pirate_pay
--     BUILD_NAVY, as public.pirate_commission), added by public.pirate_add, one every pirate_add_minutes, the old ships of 0339 first.
--   * A SEA'S PIRATES RAISE ITS RAIDS BY A CAPPED FIGURE: public.pirate_pressure_write writes least(pirate_pressure_max, pirate_pressure x ships).
--     Before: 0.5 a ship with no cap, so 40 fleets in one sea would have made every day there a raid day (danger 1). Now at most 1.0: a sea with two
--     or more pirate fleets cruising it has twice its authored danger, never more. The fight itself, the flight, the loot: untouched.
-- KNOBS: NEW pirate_respawn_minutes 60; pirate_add_minutes 10 (was navy_build_hours 24 h, which stays the navy's); pirate_pressure_max 1.0.
--   CHANGED (the owner ordered the ships; docs/dev-log has the arithmetic): pirate_spend_day_pct 0.005 -> 0.012 (the day's room of a 980 M hoard
--   4.9 M -> 11.8 M: 121 fleets' pay is 7.26 M a day). NOT changed: pirate_max, pirate_min, pirate_hoard_unit (public.pirate_size() is still 0339's).
-- NO PLAYER FIGHTS A PLAYER: nothing here touches it. NOTHING IS MINTED: every payment is public.pirate_pay, public.pay_city or a pair of
--   public.treasury_post rows of the moved kind REFIT. The five purses are 0.
-- THE RE-CUTS (hunks; each occurs exactly once in the live body and reverses to its pre-image; ACL, volatility, definer, config, owner unmoved):
--   public.pirate_ship_step (2), public.pirate_add (3), public.pirate_haunt_of (1), public.pirate_pressure_write (1), public.npc_refit_step (1),
--   world.pirate_ship_card (1). 0408 (the gift) cuts public.capital_gift_roster and public.capital_gift_one, 0410 the merchants: none of these six.
-- LOCKS: row writes on public.port_goods (ONLY the haul of the rows of the 18 goods the five offer whose nearest maker is now a hub: no stock, max stock or affinity of an
--   existing row is touched), public.sea_reaches (every row gains five keys); ALTER TABLE
--   public.pirate_ships (7 rows). lock_timeout 5 s: a trade holding one of those market rows longer rolls the file back whole. Deploy at a quiet minute.
-- BUDGET: ONE DO block, statement_timeout 120 s, lock_timeout 5 s; fails above 60 s. SELF-ASSERT: its own rows and probes only; the probe (a roster
